    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and verified. `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner API to return `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. Since `checkDigit` is purely derived from `customerCode`, I implemented it as a read-time derived field, matching how existing derived fields (`initials`, `locality`, `identityKey`, `contactPreference`) work.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`mapper/CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a standalone helper with `of(String)` that computes the Luhn check digit over the digit characters of the customer code (ignoring the `-` separators). It's a standalone class rather than a mapper method for the same reason documented on `OwnerLocality`: a single-arg method on a MapStruct mapper would be picked up as an implicit conversion.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the helper to the mapper's `imports` and a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(CustomerCodeCheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode()))\")`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.checkDigit` for the mapper to populate.\n\nThe Luhn algorithm in the helper matches the test's reference `luhn(...)` exactly (right-to-left, doubling every second digit, subtracting 9 when >9, then `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`), so `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact returned `checkDigit` \u2014 passes.",
